# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/).

## [Unreleased]

### Added
- added rng::isCryptographicallySecure(), a new virtual method letting
  callers ask whether an rng implementation's output is
  actually fit for cryptographic use - keys, tokens, salts,
  nonces, session ids; csprng now overrides it, true when
  backed by openssl, CryptGenRandom, or a successfully opened
  /dev/urandom, and false when none of those are available and
  it has fallen back to an internal prng instance instead;
  previously, on a platform with none of those (such as
  Solaris 8), csprng was permanently non-functional, since
  every generate()/generateBytes() call failed, but now it
  falls back to prng, seeded via prng::getSeed(), and keeps
  working, just without the cryptographic-security guarantee;
  csprng::isSupported() now unconditionally returns true,
  matching the existing bignumber/arc4 precedent, since a
  fallback implementation is always built in
- added singledes and tripledes classes, providing raw
  block-cipher single DES-CBC and 3-key EDE triple-DES-CBC
  transforms (no key parity checks, and padding is optional
  via setUsePadding()), for legacy protocols that need a raw
  DES or 3DES cipher rather than a modern AEAD cipher, such as
  Oracle's pre-O5LOGON authentication; singledes uses OpenSSL's
  low-level DES functions when they're available, sidestepping
  the legacy provider that OpenSSL 3.x requires for single DES
  through the EVP interface, the same way arc4 does for RC4,
  and falls back to a bundled implementation otherwise;
  tripledes uses OpenSSL's 3DES-EDE support when it's
  available, and the same bundled implementation otherwise
- added domnode::setValue(value,length) and
  domnode::setAttributeValue(name,value,length) overloads, and
  domnode::getValueLength()/getAttributeValueLength(), so a
  node or attribute value containing an embedded null byte
  can be stored and retrieved intact instead of being
  truncated; jsondom, xmldom, csvdom, inidom, and propdom now
  use the stored length rather than scanning for a null byte
  when serializing a value, and csvdom builds tree nodes
  using the length-aware csvsax field()/column() hooks so a
  parsed field or column value with an embedded null survives
  into the tree; jsondom escapes an embedded null as a JSON
  unicode escape; xmldom writes an embedded null through
  as-is, which XML 1.0 cannot represent, so the resulting
  document is not well-formed in that case
- added csvsax::field(value,length,quoted) and
  csvsax::column(name,length,quoted) overloads, and
  sax::parseString(string,length), so a field or column
  value containing an embedded null byte can reach the
  caller intact instead of being truncated
- added a bignumber class, providing arbitrary-precision signed
  integer arithmetic, wrapping OpenSSL's BIGNUM functions
  when they're built in and usable and falling back to a
  built-in implementation otherwise
- added modular arithmetic to bignumber - nonNegativeModulo(),
  modAdd(), modSub(), modMul(), modPow(), modInverse(), and gcd()
- added an arc4 class, providing the RC4 stream cipher, using OpenSSL
  when it's built in and usable and falling back to a built-in
  implementation otherwise
- added PCRE2 support, configure now prefers PCRE2, then PCRE1, then
  POSIX regex
- added an alloca check to configure for built-in-regex builds on
  non-GNU compilers
- added \g<number> and \g<name> backrefs to charstring::replace()
- added regularexpression::matchNext()
- added backref expansion (\0-\9, \\) to charstring::replace()
- added regularexpression::setPattern(pattern,options) for
  case-insensitive/multiline/dotall
- added regularexpression::getSubstringIndex(name) and name-taking
  overloads
- added regularexpression::match(str,length,offset) resuming
  mid-subject
- added sha512, aes192, aes256 classes and
  encryption::setUsePadding(bool) (SQL Relay #8976)
- added randomnumber::generateBytes() four overloads
- added a csrandomnumber class (SQL Relay #9206)
- added randomnumber's seed-first static generateBytes() overloads
- added csrandomnumber::scale(), getRandMax(), and static
  generate()/generate(lower,upper)
- added an rng base class, renamed randomnumber to prng and
  csrandomnumber to csprng, added generateBytes() methods to each

### Changed
- the sharedmemory test now waits for its child process instead of
  sleeping a second before deleting the key file the child needs,
  which raced on slow hosts, and it now folds the child's exit
  status into its own result, which it had been discarding - the
  suite reported success even when the child's assertion failed
- prng::getSeed() now mixes microseconds and the pid into the seed
  when /dev/urandom isn't available, rather than returning the
  epoch alone, which has one-second resolution and gave two
  calls in the same second the same seed
- clarified csprng::isSupported() doc comment - it reports whether a
  backend is compiled in, not whether one initialized for a
  given instance
- website ssi expanded at build time instead of by apache
- website html files not executable anymore
- regenerated doc/programming/charstring.html and xmlsax.html, which
  had gone stale against their .wt sources
- regenerated five doc/programming pages (dictionary, linkedlist,
  scalar, singlylinkedlist, table) that wt had been truncating
  (fixed under #8966)
- bumped soname librudiments.so.12 to .so.13
- stopped compiling static archives in the deb build
- stopped warning about the apache library's undefined symbols in the
  deb build
- tls class sets BIO to use lowLevelRead/Write now, when using openssl
- tls class uses SSL_CTX_set_min/max_proto_version to pin tls version when
  using openssl, if available

### Removed
- removed regularexpression::clear() - the destructor does its work
  now
- removed the bundled md5 reference implementation from the export
  list, non-openssl builds
- removed obsolete AIX "#pragma alloca" from the bundled glibc regex
  engine, built-in-regex builds
- removed bundled sha-1/sha-256/aes-128 reference implementations
  from the export list, non-openssl builds
- removed bundled regex engine from the export list on built-in-regex
  builds

### Fixed
- fixed two bugs in the bytestring fallbacks used on platforms whose
  libc lacks memmem()/memrchr(): findFirst() never tested the
  last position the needle could start at, so a needle at the
  very end of the haystack was never found, and findLast()
  started one byte past the end of the buffer, reading out of
  bounds and potentially returning a pointer past the end
- fixed csprng::isSupported() to actually check for a usable
  backend - openssl or CryptGenRandom compiled in, or
  /dev/urandom present and readable - instead of
  unconditionally returning true, so callers on a host with
  none of those, such as Solaris 8, get an honest answer
- fixed sax::getCharacter() to distinguish a real end of input
  from a literal null byte read from the underlying file,
  string, or input, so an embedded null byte no longer
  ends a csvsax parse early
- fixed segfault in file::getBaseName(filename,ext) when the base
  name doesn't end in ext, on NULL arguments, or when the base
  name is entirely the extension
- fixed double free in regularexpression::clear() on builds without
  PCRE (POSIX regex or built-in regex)
- fixed hash::reset() not clearing the hash itself
- fixed pbkdf2::reset() not clearing the salt
- fixed md5::getHash() overread when built against an openssl whose
  MD5_Final() returns int
- fixed sha1::getError() fallthrough (non-openssl builds) reporting
  success on error
- fixed sha256::clear() reporting failure on success, non-openssl
  builds
- fixed memory leaks in regularexpression::setPattern() on realloc
  failure, built-in-regex builds
- fixed memory leak in regularexpression::setPattern() on a too-big
  pattern, built-in-regex builds - unlike the leak fixed under
  #8928, this one needs no failed allocation to reach
- fixed regularexpression::match(str,length,offset) copying the whole
  subject before rejecting a bad offset, non-PCRE builds
- fixed built-in regex build warning, unused locals under -Wall
  -Werror
- fixed memory leak in regularexpression::setPattern() on failed
  compile, built-in-regex builds
- fixed charstring::replace() empty-match stepping from wrong point
- fixed charstring::replace() global substitution resume offset
- fixed regularexpression::getSubstringStart/End() pointer targets on
  non-PCRE builds
- fixed regularexpression::getSubstringCount() hiding groups after a
  non-participating one
- fixed charstring::replace() replacing only the last capture group
  instead of the whole match
- fixed datetime::parse() fractional seconds before an am/pm meridian
- fixed debian packaging dropping librudiments-apache
- fixed collection::writeValue()/writeJsonValue() printing pointers
  with %08x, truncating on LP64
- fixed FW_FIX_LIBTOOL and chmod of bin/rudiments-config not running
  via config.status
- fixed randomnumber::scale() to clamp its result to "upper"
- fixed codetree::popBreakStack() freeing a scalar-new'd break_t
  with delete[], corrupting the heap
- fixed charstring::printf(char *,size_t,const char *,va_list *) to
  va_copy() a fresh va_list for each vsnprintf() call it makes,
  rather than reusing the one passed in; on platforms whose
  vsnprintf() reports truncation by returning -1 instead of the
  needed size (Solaris, notably), the function retries with
  ever-larger buffers, and reusing an already-consumed va_list
  across those retries is undefined behavior - it could hand a
  %s conversion a stale argument pointer on a later retry,
  sending it scanning unboundedly for a NUL byte (SQL Relay
  #10021, #10022)

### Security
- fixed buffer overflow when unix socket file name is too long

## [2.2.0] - 2026-07-27

### Added
- added isSupported() to encryption/hash
- added block cipher modes to encryption and aes128
- added pbkdf2 class
- added dh class
- added date::parse() with adjustshortyears option
- added hash::getRequiredSaltSize()
- added dynamiclib::getNextSymbol() (portable RTLD_NEXT/dlvsym symbol
  wrapper)
- added dependency info to the debian/ubuntu package control file
- added Mon (mixed-case month abbreviation) format string to
  datetime::formatAs()
- added a README.md for the github mirror at
  github.com/firstworks-software/rudiments

### Changed
- made pbkdf2 build against pre-1.0.0 openssl (falls back to sha-1)

### Fixed
- fixed return value of sha256::append() when not using openssl
- fixed null-safety in charstring::findFirstIgnoringCase()
- fixed date::parse() so that NULL datedelimiters enables all delimiters
- fixed debugprintf macros to use updated methods
- fixed iconvert crash (iconv_close(-1)) when iconv_open() fails (e.g.
  native solaris iconv)
- fixed dh class build on modern LibreSSL (opaque DH struct)
- fixed statfs-style detection so NetBSD 2.x is not mis-detected as old
  FreeBSD (filesystem.cpp getTypeName failed to compile)
- fixed pthread detection on FreeBSD 15 (probe now also link-tests
  pthread_create, not just pthread_exit)

