## [2.0.0] - 2024-10-04

### Added
- added object, collection class heirarchy
- added table class
- added scalar class
- implemented degenerate wcharstring for systems that don't support
  wide characters, and added a supported() method
- added a posix semaphores implementation of semaphoreset
- added sensitivevalue class
- added configure test for Irix
- added configure test for iswblank() and alternative implementation
- added configure test for mbrtowc()/mbtowc() and implementations for
  each
- added wcharstring::copy(...const char *...) methods
- added mvcdao class
- added acfirstworks.m4 and acrudiments.m4 for other projects to use in
  their configure scripts
- added NSModule/NSObjectFileImage-based implementation of dynamiclib
- added file::getMatchingFileNames() methods
- added (w)charstring compareWithWildcard(), compareVersions(), and
  compareNatural() methods
- added comparator class with reverse and natural options, and updated
  various collections to use its methods instead of
  node_compare(), also added get/setComparator() methods to
  collection class
- added character/charstring::duplicate(wchar_t) methods to convert wide
  strings to normal strings
- added wchar_t/wchar_t * methods to a bunch of classes
- added memory-related methods to sys class
- added charstring/wcharstring::humanReadable() methods
- added filedescriptor::supportsPassReceiveFileDescriptor/Socket() and
  updated it for various systems
- added a socketlayer class below securitycontext and updated websocket
  to inherit from that
- added an int cast to a char array subscript in regex.cpp
- added some Unixware-specific libtool tweaks
- implemented copy constructors and = operators for various classes that
  they were previously hidden in
- added shutdown flag/signal framework to process class
- added SIGXCPU, SIGXFSZ and SIGPWR to the "shutdown signals"
- implemented sys::getAvailable*() for SVR5 (eg. UnixWare)
- implemented block-aligned buffering, which prefers to use mmap, but
  can fall back to traditional buffering, for non-stream
  filedescriptors
- added mvccrud interface
- added thread::reliable()
- added httpModuleInit/httpModuleExit functions
- added resourcepool class
- added encryption::getRawData() and getRawDataSize()
- added peer validation options to url class
- added getters to url class
- added duplicateFrom(Wide)CharacterNeedsMutex() methods
- implemented wcharacter/wcharstring/wstringbuffer methods for platforms
  with wstr.h
- added ucs2character/ucs2charstring/ucs2stringbuffer classes
- added iconvert class
- added printHex() to output class
- added sys::getMin/Max*() methods
- added get/set and advise to many sys methods
- added get to some directory methods
- added locale class
- added various case-insensitive replace() methods
- added *charstring::findEndOfQuotedString() methods
- added static filesystem::getOptimumTransferBlockSize()
- added support for additional openssl get-key methods

### Changed
- configure test for dirent.h includes sys/types.h too now
- in bytestring.cpp, NULL is redefined if _G_config.h undef'ed it
- changed collection paradigm from multiple remove/clearAndDelete...()
  methods to setManage...Values/Keys() methods and single
  clear()/remove()
- cleaned up httpresponse::status()
- configure script uses -Werror when detecting iov_base now
- code checks dlclose() for not -1 rather than for 0 now
- wcharstring class handles platforms that don't support vswprintf()
- updated call to GNU stderror_r to use the buffer it fills rather than
  the return value
- also updated the error class to prefer strerror() to GNU strerror_r()
  if XSI strerror_r() isn't present, as GNU strerror_r() appears
  to be flaky
- dictionarynode renamed dictionarypair
- updated comparator class to use arithmetic instead of comparisons
  where possible
- process::exitOn*() call exitImmediately() now (which is
  async-signal-safe)
- methods that retry on EINTR also check process::getShutDownFlag() now
  and return if it's true
- refactored environment a bit and added a lengthy explanation for why
  it has to do all the things that it does
- renamed isSignaHandlerIntUsed to supportsSignalHandlerParameter
- refactored write methods of dom class and its children a bit
- yday->mday in datetime::setDays()
- filedescriptor::printf() methods return ssize_t now
- refactored mvcresult a bit
- httpserverapi and httprequest are inputs now
- dom and children's write*() methods return the number of bytes written
  now, instead of just true/false
- de-consted most things
- datetime initializes mday, wday, and yday to 1 now, fixing the
  behavior of various setters
- normalized datetime getter/setter names
- codetree writes to an output rather than stringbuffer now
- refactored crypt as a child of encryption
- datetime class sets timezone during instantiation now
- renamed some datetime methods from get*() to initFrom*()
- renamed some datetime methods from *DateAndTime() to *DateTime()
- renamed some datetime methods from adjust*() to set*()
- renamed *entry methods from init() to open()
- refactored *client and *util methods, removed convenience methods
- renamed randomnumber::generate*() to generate(), etc.
- made Filename/FileName consistent to FileName
- client connect tries defaults to 1 intead of 0 (infinite tries) now
- character::duplicate() and charstring::duplicate() use ? as the default
  replacement character now
- refactored FW_CHECK_HEADERS_AND_LIBS a bit
- url::useHttpPost/Get() -> url::setUseHttpPost()
- renamed crypt class to des
- filedescriptor::printf(const char */const wchar_t *) to stdout/stderr
  respect locale now
- converted unsigned char to byte_t
- needsMutex -> getNeedsMutex
- refactored buffer class setPosition*() methods
- moved safePrint() and printBits() to output class
- des class inherits from hash instead of encryption now
- replaced all ssize_t parameters with size_t
- renamed sys::lock/unlock to disablePaging/enablePaging
- renamed lots of methods to start with action verbs or at least "is"
- renamed lots of do/dont*() methods to just set*() and added getters
  for ones that were missing
- configure prefers /usr/bin and /usr/sbin for apr-*-config scripts now
- -Wno-overloaded-virtual is now set when clang or gcc is used
- sys::getMaxLineLength() returns 2048 instead of SSIZE_MAX if
  _SC_LINE_MAX is not supported now
- renamed row to record in csvsax and csvdom classes
- isInSet*() return false now if the set is NULL or empty

### Removed
- removed namevaluepairs/constnamevaluepairs typedefs
- removed bounds checking from various operator[] methods
- removed cursordomnode class
- removed \b support from codetree
- removed foreign append()/write() methods from *stringbuffer classes
- removed *buffer::appendFormatted() methods, preferring printf()

### Fixed
- various semi-obscure internal fixes to dictionary class
- fixed epoll_wait() and kevent() timeout detection
- fixed wprintf() -> swprintf() calls in wcharstring class
- added fixes for older OpenSSL
- fixed a few size -> length parameters
- fixed bugs in dynamicarray::clear()
- fixed memory leak in avltree clear()
- fixed some formatting bugs in datetime::formatAs()
- fixed a Werror-detection bug in the configure script for
  cross-compilers
- fixed segfault in charstring::replace()
- fixed Content-Type in url class when using curl
- fixed ininitialized mutex in crypt class
- fixed tm_isdst handling to deal with > 1 and < 0 cases
- fixed configure test for crypt_r which always reported not found
- fixed potential crash in charstring::duplicate(wchar_t)
- fixed timezone issues on UnixWare/Irix
- fixed various longstanding NULL-related bugs in compare*() methods

